[00:00] [scene:intro]
VISUAL: Jack Dorsey's tweet about self-hosting Buzz is shown.
AUDIO: 'A couple of weeks ago, I told you my Buzz wasn\'t on Block\'s servers. It\'s on mine. I never showed you how. Then last week, Jack Dorsey posted about self-hosting Buzz, and 400,000 people saw it. So let\'s fix that today.'

[00:13] [scene:speaker]
VISUAL: The presenter introduces the topic of self-hosting Buzz AI.
AUDIO: 'Your own Buzz relay, on your own hosting. Watch this. I paste one key in, I click deploy. And by the time I\'ve stopped talking, you\'ve got a place your team can work that Block isn\'t hosting, and you control the door to. Right. Let\'s go. All right. Let me back up for 30 seconds.'

[00:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'If you\'ve downloaded the Buzz desktop app, you haven\'t hosted anything. The app is a client. It\'s a window. You\'re a guest on somebody else\'s server. The relay is the server.'

[00:39] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Buzz AI chat interface showing real-time transcription.
AUDIO: 'The relay holds your messages, your files, your membership list. Right now you\'re probably using Buzz on a hosted Block server. After today, it can be you hosting that server. Now let me show you the moment this stopped being theoretical for me.'

[00:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Now think about where the transcript lives. Every word your team said sits in a database on somebody\'s server. So here\'s my rule. And I said it last week.'

[01:05] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Buzz AI interface showing channels and projects.
AUDIO: 'I run three relays, my free community, which is on Block\'s servers on purpose. It\'s an open playground where anyone can talk and walk in and Block shoulder the infra for me. I\'m not going to pay to host strangers.'

[01:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'But my business relay here, Creator Magic Ops. That\'s mine. Client work, team huddles. Anything I wouldn\'t put in a public channel. That\'s the one I hold. So, open door, let Block have it. If it\'s your business, your clients, your paying community, host it yourself.'

[01:30] [scene:speaker]
VISUAL: The presenter discusses the importance of self-hosting for business.
AUDIO: 'Now, before we go ahead and deploy, one quick warning: on your own relay, you have to trust the people you let in. They can upload, they can generate, they\'re spending your resources. And that\'s the trade.'

[01:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'You get control, but you also get the bill. And my third relay. That\'s the one for my Skool community. Private members only. Exactly the one we\'re building today. That\'s where I\'m sharing compute, the source code of apps I make. And very soon, my complete Buzz setup.'

[01:58] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Railway website displaying the Buzz template with Redis, Buzz, Postgres, and MinIO services.
AUDIO: 'Link is in the description. So where does it live? Well, this is Railway, and it\'s hosting where you don\'t touch a server. So no terminal, no SSH, no Linux. You click a button. It builds the thing.'

[02:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
